(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Controlled responses and finite-support observability limits in Rule 30\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["Troy Lowry; OpenAI Codex \[Bullet] 2026-10-24", "Author",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["\<\
Responses of a right half to every left-boundary input are characterized \
exactly by two observations of a triangular diagonal map. Terminal rewrites \
011 to 01 and 101 to 11 preserve the complete center trace with every common \
initial left half. Explicit eight-periodic infinite tails show that OR alone \
need not recover the head and that a period-two head need not detect a full \
period-eight state. Finite feedback can erase an initial distinction even \
when the common output is not eventually constant. A checked finite-profile \
certificate also proves head-period detection for every finite width at full \
clock sixteen. Finite-tail completeness and the Rule 30 Prize problems remain \
open.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Scope and provenance", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["\<\
This is a partial contribution developed by Troy Lowry with OpenAI Codex. It \
builds on the kit's driven right half in Rule30Ether and whole-line evolution \
in Rule30Realization. No literature-priority claim is made. The essay is \
prepared for human review and has not been sent to the prize API.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["\<\
The terminal rewrites can change a finite row's right edge without changing \
its center trace. For example, the two rows with black cells only at \
positions {2,3} and {2}, respectively, have identical center traces at every \
time. Their left edges agree; this does not refute recovering a left edge \
from the trace. The general theorem allows every common initial left half and \
every shared finite prefix before the displayed terminal word.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["Exact response equivalence", "Section",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell["\<\
Index a right-half state x by 0,1,\[Ellipsis] for physical positions 1,2,\
\[Ellipsis] . Define\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["\<\
    Q(x)(k) = x(k) XOR (x(k+1) OR x(k+2)).     F_b(x)  = (b XOR (x(0) OR \
x(1))) :: Q(x).\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["\<\
The second formula is exactly one Rule 30 step with left boundary bit b. Two \
right states have equal head outputs for every boundary-input sequence and \
every time if and only if, for every n, both the head and the OR of the first \
two cells of Q^n(x) agree. The infinite response tree is therefore replaced \
by two observations along one deterministic orbit. The theorem places no \
finite-support restriction on this equivalence.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["\<\
For every common finite prefix, terminal 011 followed by zeros can be \
replaced by 01, and terminal 101 followed by zeros by 11. Both replacements \
preserve responses to all boundary inputs for all times. A separate induction \
shows that this equivalence remains sound with actual feedback through the \
center: if initial left halves, including the center, agree, they agree at \
every later time. Thus both terminal rewrites preserve the complete center \
trace in the full Rule 30 system, including when both starting rows are \
finite.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell["\<\
No converse from a single prescribed driver is proved. In fact, right states \
1 and 11 have the same head output forever under the constantly zero driver, \
but are not universally response equivalent. This driver is not asserted to \
extend to a finite whole-line orbit. A second example, packed states 42 and \
70, agrees through thirteen observations for every driver but is not \
universally equivalent. Checking only 2W-1 observations is insufficient at \
W=7.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell["A finite actual-feedback counterexample", "Section",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell["\<\
There is a stronger failure of the converse from one realized input. Let the \
common initial left half, including the center, be all white, and put black \
cells at {1} in one row and {1,2} in the other. Their initial right halves 1 \
and 11 are not universally response equivalent. With the white initial \
center, one step sends them to 11 and 101. The terminal rewrite above proves \
these new right halves universally equivalent. The entire left halves still \
agree, so feedback soundness applies at every subsequent time.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell["\<\
Thus both the complete center traces and complete right-head traces agree \
forever, although the initial controlled response classes differ. Both starts \
are finite and nonzero. The kit's finite-configuration version of Jen's \
period-one result proves that neither common trace is eventually constant. \
This is an actual whole-line feedback example, without assuming an externally \
constant input. Their left edges are both position 1, so it does not refute \
left-edge recovery. No claim about their eventual periodicity is made.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell["Why the support and observation hypotheses matter", "Section",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell["\<\
Write an infinite row from its head toward the right. The two starts\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell["    x = 1100(1101)\[Ellipsis]     y = 0110(01)\[Ellipsis]", "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell["\<\
use parenthesized blocks repeated forever. Both complete Q orbits have period \
dividing eight. Their head traces differ, but the OR of the first two cells \
is the same nonconstant sequence at every time. At time two, the next OR, of \
cells one and two, differs. The common OR alone cannot recover the head or \
the next OR. These states are not universally response equivalent, because \
that relation observes the head as well.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell["\<\
A third start, 1100(0001)\[Ellipsis], has a head trace of least period two, \
whereas its complete Q orbit has least period eight. All three starts are \
proved to have infinite support. A power-of-two orbit period cannot replace \
finite support in a proposed head-period detection theorem. No finite-tail \
conjecture is refuted or proved by these examples.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["\<\
The proofs use explicit temporal profile tables, verify their scalar update \
at every depth, and then identify all iterates by induction. The finite \
search that found the tables is not a proof premise. No part of this essay \
excludes an eventual center period or proves a Rule 30 Prize problem.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["A local clock obstruction with explicit hypotheses", "Section",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell["\<\
Let five temporal columns a,b,c,d,e obey the triangular update, so the next a \
is a XOR (b OR c), the next b is b XOR (c OR d), and the next c is c XOR (d \
OR e). Put H=2n. Assume a has period 2H, b reverses color after H, and c and \
d each have period H. Then a OR b cannot have period H. Any additional \
predecessor whose temporal difference is a OR b cannot have period H either. \
There is a direct application to columns of the actual Q orbit with every \
clock assumption retained.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell["\<\
The proof supposes the OR has period H. Since b reverses after H, the OR \
would have to be constantly black. Define K(t)=a(t) XOR a(t+H). The local \
updates force d(t) to be at most c(t), and K XOR b would alternate each step. \
It would then be both H-periodic and color-reversing after the even number H \
of steps, which is impossible.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell["\<\
This protects the neighborhood of a clock onset. It does not prove arbitrary \
prefix propagation, a finite-tail period-detection theorem, or center-column \
nonperiodicity. In particular, the even half-clock and full-clock premises \
must not be dropped. No literature-priority claim is made.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell["A fixed-clock theorem covering every finite width", "Section",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell["\<\
There is now a positive finite-tail result at full clock sixteen. For every \
finitely supported x with Q^16(x)=x, any eventual head period H is a period \
of the entire state: Q^H(x)=x. The spatial width, the transient, and H are \
arbitrary. The full-clock assumption is retained explicitly. This is a \
triangular-orbit theorem, rather than a statement about a vertical center.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell["\<\
The proof checks a pool of 68 pairs of temporal profiles. Every pair in the \
pool has either no consistent predecessor column at this full clock, or both \
possible predecessors are again in the pool. Starting from the finite zero \
tail, induction covers every finite spatial width. A second check propagates \
a head period through every pair. All head-clock residues modulo sixteen are \
checked, and periodicity reduces every natural H to its residue. A purely \
periodic orbit turns any eventual head period into a period from time zero, \
so no transient bound is needed.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell["\<\
The finite search that generated the pool is not trusted. The generic Lean \
checker proves the soundness of the closure and detection checks; the \
concrete checks are evaluated by the kernel. This establishes neither an \
arbitrary-full-clock induction nor a center-column prize result. The earlier \
infinite-tail period-loss example satisfies the full-clock bound and \
illustrates why the finite-support premise matters.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell["An unbounded clock statement for the known terminal rewrites", "Section",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two terminal rewrites preserve more than the observed response. Behind \
every shared finite prefix, their complete Q-state orbits have exactly the \
same equality relations: Q",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"s", 
     RowBox[{"(", "x", ")"}]}], "=", "Q"}]]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 "t(x) if and only if Q",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"s", 
     RowBox[{"(", "y", ")"}]}], "=", "Q"}]]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 "t(y), for every s and t. In particular Q^H(x)=x if and only if Q^H(y)=y, \
for every H. There is no full-clock bound in this statement."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell["\<\
The proof uses the two tails [a,not a,1] and [a,1]. One Q step switches a and \
updates both prefixes equally. An indexed relation records the prefix length. \
Inserting or deleting the terminal cell reconstructs either linked state from \
the other, and the relation survives every Q step. The same conclusion \
follows for any finite chain of the sound rewrites.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell["\<\
Thus these known response collisions themselves preserve the full temporal \
clock. Completeness is still missing: the argument does not establish that \
every finite response collision is generated by these rewrites. No arbitrary \
head-period detection theorem or vertical-center result follows here.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell["Independent finite controls", "Section",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell["\<\
The first calculation compares terminal rewrites in 104 complete Rule 30 \
experiments with random common left halves and prefixes. The second compares \
all three profile tables with built-in Rule 30 on finite causal cones. The \
third checks eight actual-feedback examples, including the all-white left \
half, at both the center and the right head through time 128. The fourth \
checks 192 qualifying clock cases among 512 finite starts and compares ten \
whole-row Q evolutions with built-in Rule 30 on slanted causal cones. The \
fifth independently checks eight further cones for finite tails whose widths \
extend well beyond the clock bound. The sixth checks both sides of the \
terminal correspondence against sixteen built-in Rule 30 cones, comparing \
26,264 scalar cells. Separate Python controls check 1,122,302 state pairs, \
including 256 wide prefixes. These controls do not replace the unbounded \
kernel proofs.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "Independent", " ", "finite", " ", "samples", " ", "using", " ", "the", " ",
      "built"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"in", " ", "Rule", " ", "30", " ", 
     RowBox[{"evolution", ".", "\n", "   ", "Unbounded"}], " ", "statements", 
     " ", "and", " ", "feedback", " ", "soundness", " ", "are", " ", "proved",
      " ", "in", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Lean", "."}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "controlledResponseReport", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"controlledResponseReport", "[", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "20261024", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", "cases", "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cases", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{
                  "left", ",", " ", "prefix", ",", " ", "old", ",", " ", 
                   "new", ",", " ", "ca", ",", " ", "cb", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"center", " ", "=", " ", "8"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
                  "      ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"left", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"RandomInteger", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "9"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
                  "      ", 
                  RowBox[{"prefix", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"RandomInteger", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
                  "      ", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"old", ",", " ", "new"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"If", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"rule", " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
                    "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
                  RowBox[{"ca", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
                    RowBox[{"CellularAutomaton", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"30", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"left", ",", " ", "prefix", ",", " ", "old"}], 
                    "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"128", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", "center", "}"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}],
                   ";", "\n", "      ", 
                  RowBox[{"cb", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
                    RowBox[{"CellularAutomaton", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"30", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"left", ",", " ", "prefix", ",", " ", "new"}], 
                    "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"128", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", "center", "}"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}],
                   ";", "\n", "      ", 
                  RowBox[{"<|", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"\<PrefixLength\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "n"}], ",",
                     " ", 
                    RowBox[{"\"\<Rewrite\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"If", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"rule", " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", 
                    " ", "\"\<011->01\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<101->11\>\""}], 
                    "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
                    RowBox[{"\"\<Horizon\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "128"}], ",", 
                    " ", 
                    RowBox[{"\"\<ObservationCount\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"Length", "[", "ca", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"\"\<SameCenterTracePrefix\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"SameQ", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"ca", ",", " ", "cb"}], "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}]}], 
                "\n", "    ", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
               " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"sample", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], 
              "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"<|", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"\"\<FiniteSamplesOnly\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",",
             " ", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<UnboundedProofReplaced\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
             "False"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<FullProblemClaim\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], ",",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<CaseCount\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "cases", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<AllPassed\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"And", "@@", 
              RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
               RowBox[{"cases", ",", " ", "\"\<SameCenterTracePrefix\>\""}], 
               "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<Cases\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "cases"}]}], "|>"}]}]}], 
        "\n", "  ", "]"}]}], "\n", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
    "Compare", " ", "all", " ", "three", " ", "infinite", " ", "profile", " ",
      "tables", " ", "with", " ", "actual", " ", "finite", " ", "Rule", " ", 
     "30", " ", 
     RowBox[{"cones", "."}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "profileCounterReport", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"profileCounterReport", "[", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"tables", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"h", " ", "=", " ", "32"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"window", " ", "=", " ", "8"}], ",", " ", "counts"}], "}"}], 
       ",", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"tables", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
            "45", ",", "43", ",", "186", ",", "166", ",", "101", ",", "149", ",",
              "86", ",", "89"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
            "42", ",", "45", ",", "51", ",", "170", ",", "170", ",", "85", ",",
              "170", ",", "85"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
            "85", ",", "87", ",", "168", ",", "212", ",", "172", ",", "178", ",",
              "202", ",", "43"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
        RowBox[{"counts", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
              "profile", ",", " ", "n", ",", " ", "initial", ",", " ", "ca", ",",
                " ", "checks"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"profile", "[", "k_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"table", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"If", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"k", "<", "4"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"k", "+", "1"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"5", "+", 
                    RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"k", "-", "4"}], ",", "4"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
                 "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
              RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"window", "+", 
                RowBox[{"2", "*", "h"}], "+", "2"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
              RowBox[{"initial", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"BitAnd", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"profile", "[", "k", "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}],
                  ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
              "    ", 
              RowBox[{"ca", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"CellularAutomaton", "[", 
